# Generated by Codery — setup session with Tural, 2026-08-11. Amend via issues in this repo.
#
# These rules exist to keep dataset text out of git. Datasets, checkpoints, caches,
# and run output are re-downloadable or re-creatable; git holds code, configs,
# metrics, and notes. The patterns catch the common cases — the behavioral rule in
# CLAUDE.md is what actually binds. If you find yourself adding an exception for a
# data file, stop.

# Dataset directories — re-downloaded, never committed. Kept apart from the extension
# rules below because a negation cannot rescue anything inside an ignored directory.
data/
Data/
DATA/
datasets/

# Dataset text by extension — real distributions ship under any filename
# (musique_ans_v1.0_train.jsonl, qa_train_2hop.txt, kb.txt), so match the extension,
# not the name. The negations for small committed files are at the bottom of this
# file and must stay after these rules.
*.jsonl
*.tsv
*.csv
*.txt

# Model checkpoints and weights — too large for git; they live on the compute box.
# `models/` is anchored to the repo root: unanchored, it also matched
# components/router/models/ and components/decomposer/models/, which hold per-model
# prompts and configs — committed source, and silently uncommittable until this was
# anchored. The negations below are belt-and-braces for the same trap.
/models/
checkpoints/
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.bin

# Run output — regenerated by re-running the experiment; the log entry is the record.
runs/
outputs/
*.log

# Embedding / feature caches — derived data, rebuilt on demand.
.cache/
cache/
embeddings/
*.npy
*.npz
*.faiss

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Virtualenvs
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Notebook checkpoints
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Secrets / env
.env
.env.*

# Gate telemetry — local record of hook decisions, not repo history.
.gate-telemetry.jsonl

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Small files that must stay committable. Negations go last, after every pattern they
# exempt. They cannot rescue anything inside an ignored directory (data/, runs/,
# outputs/, models/, cache/) — which is why committed run artifacts live under
# experiments/<exp-id>/ and heavy output stays in runs/.
!configs/**
!docs/**
!experiments/**/*.json
!experiments/**/*.yaml
!experiments/**/*.yml
!experiments/**/*.md
!requirements*.txt
!*.md

# Text that is source, not data. The `*.txt` rule above catches dataset dumps, but a
# prompt file or a run's own text output is source and would otherwise vanish with no
# trace — an ignored file never appears in `git status`, so the mistake is silent.
!**/prompt*.txt
!experiments/**/*.txt

# Per-model component assets: prompt templates and configs, one folder per model.
# These are experimental assets (the prompt text must stay byte-identical to v1), so
# they must never be caught by a checkpoint or data pattern.
#
# Negated by extension, not with a blanket `**`: a blanket negation would also rescue a
# stray *.safetensors / *.npy / bulk *.jsonl dropped into a model folder, which is
# exactly the weight-and-data traffic the rules above exist to stop. Only the two
# extensions these folders actually hold are exempt.
!components/**/models/
!components/**/models/**/
!components/**/models/**/*.md
!components/**/models/**/*.json

# Synthetic smoke-test fixtures. Every byte under tests/fixtures/ is hand-written and
# fabricated — no rows are copied from MuSiQue or MetaQA — so it is source, not data.
# Without these negations the .txt / .jsonl rules above would silently swallow the only
# executable verification the pipeline has before real data exists.
#
# Also negated by extension: fixtures are small hand-written files, so a *.safetensors,
# *.npy or *.pt appearing under this tree means something went wrong and must stay
# ignored rather than be quietly committable.
!tests/fixtures/
!tests/fixtures/**/
!tests/fixtures/**/*.md
!tests/fixtures/**/*.json
!tests/fixtures/**/*.jsonl
!tests/fixtures/**/*.txt
!tests/fixtures/**/*.csv

# Jahid's personal working note, kept local by design — not pipeline code or docs.
Plan\ after\ the\ meeting.md
